    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/getting-started.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "1. Read the facts — mechanical, read-only, before anything is written",
      "prov:value": "`describeRepository()` (`schemas/content/content-type.ts`) returns every\n> marker a repository carries — `folio`, `harness`, `dak`, `sushi` — with the\n> facts each states and any disagreement between them.\n> `describeRepositoryClosure()` (`schemas/kg/harness-config.ts`) extends that\n> through the dependency tree, attributing each membership to the instance\n> that carried it. Bean `79t3`.\n>\n> **`folio` and `harness` are different types, and the distinction is load-\n> bearing here.**",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 79t3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/getting-started.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "3. Ask — as options, never as prose",
      "prov:value": "**Put a harness on the remote repository (`written-to`)** — instantiate the\n   harness in that remote repository itself and build in its own CI\n   (`stage-ig-sites --only <instance> --source .`), only after explicit\n   permission for that repository. Bean `b5f0`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean b5f0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/getting-started.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "4. Route",
      "prov:value": "**An empty repository gets `main` before any feature branch.** GitHub makes\nthe first branch pushed to an empty repository its default, so run\n`init-folio` (it seeds `main` first) or push `main` yourself before pushing\nanything else. litlfred/dth-hrh got a feature branch as its default this way\n(owner, 2026-10-14).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-14",
        "owner"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/getting-started.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "4. Route",
      "prov:value": "Where `folio_init` does not\nhandle that content type directly, the new-repository route scaffolds with\n`--instance`. Bean `3tza`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 3tza"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/getting-started.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "5. After scaffolding — seed the plan, then publish",
      "prov:value": "2. **Provision `gh-pages` — before Pages is switched on.** This is\n   `Task_ProvisionGhPages` in the process, and it carries the semantics of\n   `A_Provision` in bootstrap-tools'\n   [`render-kg-to-github-pages.bpmn`](../../../../bootstrap-tools/processes/render-kg-to-github-pages.bpmn)\n   (the `gh-pages` Tool's subprocess —\n   [`render-kg-to-cdn`](../../process/workflow/render-kg-to-cdn.md)):\n   **a `gh-pages` branch must exist before Pages can be switched on** to serve\n   it. Owner, 2026-10-01: *\"need to create gh-pages branch before can turn\n   on\"*; repeated 2026-10-07: *\"need to create gh-pages before can deploy\"*\n   (issue #2417). Run\n   `bun run cat-harness-tools/scripts/pages-bootstrap.ts --provision`: it checks\n   `git ls-remote --heads origin gh-pages` and, only if the branch is absent,\n   pushes an orphan `gh-pages` holding a placeholder `index.html` and\n   `.nojekyll`. It is idempotent and never forces a push; without\n   `--provision` the script creates no remote branch, it only reports\n   `unprovisioned` with the exact command. Then switch Pages on with\n   **Source: \"Deploy from a branch: gh-pages, / (root)\"** — not \"GitHub\n   Actions\", when the publish workflow pushes `gh-pages` (the script prints\n   the source it expects). **Every publishing route reaches this step**:\n   new-repo, add-folio, and the overlay route through\n   [`repo-conversion`](repo-conversion.md) — including an overlay or new repo\n   that [remote-mounts](../../kg/kg-core/remote-mount.md) its dependencies,\n   which never reaches this section by itself.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#2417",
        "2026-10-01",
        "2026-10-07",
        "owner"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-01",
        "2026-10-07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/getting-started.md#provenance-6",
